| R92 | A report's before/after receipt labels identify the driver digest and exact measured revision carried by that receipt, not a later tip or earlier driver variant. A process exit is claimed only when the receipt captures its terminal rc. Commit-to-LOG ties use existing bullet text or indices, never invented labels; an omitted commit is appended as a correction. | Round65 non-author spotcheck routed defects1–6, corrected in corpus/lessons/round-66.md. Its old base receipts lack a terminal rc and the report labelled driver5aa842ab as final7f27c4d2. Round66 controls/red-before-mechanism.txt explicitly captures audit_rc0 and terminal exit0; the historical omission is not retroactively fixed. |

## Round-67 additions — payload expectations, native faces, one writer per control (append-only)

R6 form: every line above keeps its number; this block is appended after R92. Each row closes a
round-67 Mistakes row (`corpus/lessons/round-67.md` § Mistakes).

| id | criterion | grounded in |
|---|---|---|
| R93 | A wave payload's expected verdicts are re-derived from the production bytes before dispatch, and a payload line the measured base matrix contradicts is corrected in a committed addendum that every affected seat receives — the payload file itself is preserved, never rewritten after it is taken. Check: the addendum names the contradicted line and the measured line beside it. | M67-1: the round-67 payload froze `P1/P2 base rc0` (production already carries round-66's cat repair) and `P8 candidate derive-upstream-signal-13` (P8's native stage0 is 0, so no candidate can derive a signal). Both were corrected by `.ufo/waves/round-67/controls/dispatch-addendum-r67.md` before the seats froze their batteries. |
| R94 | A probe whose native status is not stable across repeats is not frozen to one reason or one base verdict: the claim asserts the verdict, the receipt records the face, and the counter loops until it observes the −13 face before counting a repair. | M67-2: `wc -l big.txt missing.txt | head -n 1` measured −13 five of five in one pass and 1 in another; `grep` yields −13 or 2 depending on which side of the race wins; the frozen rows became verdict-level with an any-of reason set and a `FACE` line per attempt. |
| R95 | An option/operand classifier in a gate applies end-of-options semantics at the FIRST `--` anywhere in the decoded argv, not only at position 0, and the probe set carries the mid-argv spelling. Check: a dash-named operand after a mid-argv `--` reads stale at the candidate and ok at the base. | M67-3: the critic measured `cut -f1 -d: big.txt -- -missing.txt | head -n 1` reading `ok` at the first candidate while `-missing.txt` was never opened (native −13 five of five); the differential without `--` exits 1 because cut treats the token as an unknown option. |
| R96 | A counter's sub-assertions distinguish a bound instrument from an ignored one: a diagnostic line from a bound collector is recorded as a finding, never scored as a harness failure. | M67-4: the first round-67 `--final` failed `multihead-mutbat` because `COLLECTOR unstable=P10` (the collector's own legitimate finding) was read as `collector-ignored`; erratum 1 narrowed the assertion to a literal ` ignored=` line plus a required `probes=collector:` binding. |
| R97 | A pinned control has exactly one writer. The L1 freezes control bytes before pinning them; an edit to a pinned control after the pinning commit is reverted and recorded, and a seat that needs a control change asks for a bounded unfreeze. | M67-5 and M67-10: the mutation battery was edited by the seat and by the L1 in the same window (a duplicated `WC_REASONS` definition had to be removed), and a post-commit edit left the worktree at a digest the pins did not carry. |
| R98 | Every digest written into a frozen claims record is recomputed from the committed bytes at freeze time, never transcribed from an earlier worktree reading. Check: the claims digest equals the digest of the file at the named controls revision. | M67-6: `claims.json` recorded the battery as `e6d54540…` while the commit and the pins carried `88e0c3e6…`; corrected by `claims-erratum-1.md` E2. |
| R99 | The final measurement is written to its receipt file by the same command that runs it (`> controls/final-verification-r<NN>.txt`), and a run whose output was only read on a terminal is recorded as a process miss, never reconstructed. | M67-9: the first round-67 `--final` ran without a redirect; only its `RESULT`/`VERIFY` lines survived in the transcript and the failing measurement's full receipt had to be copied out of the scratch tree separately. |
| R100 | A source row's anchor digest is the normalized snapshot digest or a byte-stable artifact's digest; a raw response digest that varies between fetches of the same page is recorded as a nonce-bound instance digest and never carried into a row. | M67-8: the round-65 lead pinned the FIRST maturity page's raw HTML digest `334aeb01…`, which six fetches could not reproduce (per-response CSP nonce, identical 82978-byte length, one normalized digest); the lead is retired as S100/S101 with the correction stated in `corpus/SOURCES.md`. |

Round-69 criteria (appended 2026-11-04), each grounded in a round-69 Mistakes row (`corpus/lessons/round-69.md` § Mistakes).

| id | criterion | grounded in |
|---|---|---|
| R101 | A receipt or claim that names a host tool's identity names the binary the instrument actually executes, resolved the way the instrument resolves argv[0] (from the instrument's own process, not the operator shell). Check: the counter's `HOST` line and the receipt's tool statement agree. | M69-1: round-68 statements called the gate's sort "uutils 0.8.0" from the omp shell builtin while the gate runs `/usr/bin/sort` GNU coreutils 9.12 (`.ufo/waves/round-69/controls/c1-base-donothing-r69.txt` HOST line). |
| R102 | A frontier freeze that opens more than one candidate source states its registry after-count as before + admitted rows + contract-required rejected rows (CORPUS.md: rejected sources are rows with status `rejected`). Check: the frozen `registry=` value minus the before value equals the number of opened candidates the round lands as rows. | M69-2: round-69 C2 froze `registry=103` counting S103 only; the opened-and-refused EUVD candidate went to the Search log instead of a `rejected` row. |
| R103 | Every refusal rule added to a parse gate carries a selftest case that fails when that rule alone is removed (one-limb mutant killed), including the empty-operand and end-of-options limbs. Check: the one-limb mutant set over the new rules is killed by the selftest. | `.ufo/waves/round-69/controls/l1-mutation-r69.txt`: 9/11 killed; M9 (drop the `--` limb) and M10 (drop the no-operand limb of `git_show_operands_ok`) survive because no case pins `git show` with no operand or with `--`. |
| R104 | A row inserted into a markdown table is verified by counting the table's rows before and after the edit; the after count must be before+1, and no pre-existing row may disappear. Check: `grep -cE '^\| F[0-9]+ \|' corpus/README.md` (or the registry's row pattern) on both sides of the edit. | M70-1: the round-70 README edit for F48 was written as a whole-row replacement and deleted the F47 row in the working tree; only the row count would have caught it before commit. |
| R105 | A capture lands in the same commit as the `manifest.json` that binds it; a tracked snapshot directory is never created before its manifest exists. Check: `capture-binding-check.py` prints no `FAIL rule=missing-manifest`, and any base counter measured while such a directory exists is re-measured. | M70-2: `corpus/source-snapshots/round-70/` existed with `S105.txt` and no manifest while the C2 base counters ran, so `capture-binding-check.py` printed `FAIL rule=missing-manifest dir=round-70` and the base receipt was polluted. |
| R106 | A counter whose ledger derives are `git show <rev>:<path>` runs on a checkout or clone with a git object store, never on a `git archive` export, and the receipt names which closure it used. Check: `real-ledger` reads `figures=35 ok=35 stale=0` in the final receipt. | M70-3: the first round-70 final run used a `git archive` export of `c1051749` and read `figures=35 ok=11 stale=24` (exit 1); the same counter on a `git clone --shared` checkout of that revision read 35/35 (exit 0). |
| R107 | A receipt named in a frozen pins file is never overwritten after the freeze; a re-measurement lands as a new receipt file and the frozen bytes stay byte-identical. Check: `sha256sum` of every pinned receipt equals its pins line at the evidence commit. | M70-5: `controls/c2-after-counters-r70.txt` was pinned at `e74ba6b5` (`f20fd6e7…`) and then rewritten with the shared-clone measurement, so the pinned hash and the committed file disagreed until the frozen bytes were restored and the re-measurement landed as `…-clone.txt`. |
| R108 | A knowledge entry attributes only what its anchors state; a generalization the page does not make is either marked as the entry's reading or dropped, and a critic seat's outrun list is applied before the round closes. Check: every sentence with a `(S###.txt:N)` anchor is a quote or an explicit paraphrase of that line, and the round's erratum names the old→new entry hash. | M70-7: `CriticC2` listed 21 outruns in the round-70 F48 entry (a three-class count the page never states, a fix-version sentence whose subject is "malware alerts", an inverted CVSS-provenance branch, one misquote and an inverted author cell), corrected in `.ufo/waves/round-70/controls/pins-r70-erratum-1.txt`. |
| R109 | A receipt is hashed and pinned only after the process that writes it has exited; no commit or freeze is made while a background writer is still producing receipts. Check: every pins line equals the blob at the freeze commit and the working-tree file. | M70-8: the controls commit `15d4da87` and the freeze `e74ba6b5` captured `controls/c1-forgery-blanket-r70.txt` mid-write (10-line truncated blob `fdbcc484…`), while the pin (`d74ba3f9…`) described the completed file that only landed at `7f6e39a9`. |

| R110 | A round signals done only after the lane's quiescence gate passes: `git -C <lane> status --porcelain` prints nothing (no uncommitted round work, no stray untracked file at the round's end) and the D1 placeholder clause of `bash corpus/instruments/r35-defect-closure.sh` reports no `filled by the L1` line in `SCORECARD.md`. Check: both commands' output is pasted in the round report and the lane tip is the reported hash. | `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` proposal 3 (operator reflection, 2026-10-26: "Add a quiescence gate before `complete`"); round-35's rejection reintroduced a `filled by the L1` placeholder at `SCORECARD.md:1271` and round-70's closure carried no uncommitted work but the class had no pre-commit gate before this row. |
